# 3D Beam Analysis

This section contains the finite element analysis of the beam using 3D solid elements in ANSYS Mechanical.

## Analysis

The beam was modelled as a three-dimensional solid geometry and analyzed under the specified loading and boundary conditions.

The analysis was performed to determine:

- Total deformation
- Equivalent (von-Mises) stress

The 3D FEA results were compared with the analytical solution and the results obtained from the 1D beam-element model.

## Purpose

The 3D model provides a more detailed representation of the actual beam geometry and allows the stress and deformation response to be evaluated using 3D solid elements.

